  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Human Rights and Environmental Protection</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project was formerly run by the Vicariate of Juli, but due to the lack of support from the Bishop for their work, the Vicariate closed in December 2007 and a new independent NGO was set up in January 2008. The partner has been involved in human rights work in Peru since the 1980s during the time of the civil war (1980-2000). It worked to publicise the Truth and Reconciliation Commission that was published in 2003, provided detailed information about the abuses committed and put pressure on the government to implement its recommendations. The partner also works to empower the local community to participate in politics. Now the partner focuses on working with communities affected by mining and climate change to defend their land rights and the environment.</narrative>
  </description>
